type: software
title: "guides: reproducible CRISPRi guide context in K562"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
authors:
  - family-names: Klarov
    given-names: Leonid
    email: leonid.klarov@gmail.com
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A small terminal program that places Dolcetto or user-supplied CRISPRi
  spacers in a human GRCh38 locus and generates a reproducible Quarto report
  of annotated promoters and K562 DNase, histone-mark and CTCF peak overlaps.
keywords:
  - CRISPRi
  - K562
  - reproducibility
  - genomic annotation
